Chapter: ShadowKernel
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceEffect
  cites Gpu chapter DeviceMath

 Ray-traced soft shadows as a [Device] compute kernel. The same three-sphere,
 checkered-floor scene, lit by an overhead AREA light: each pixel that sees a
 surface casts a 3x3 grid of shadow rays toward points spread across the light
 disk and averages the visibility, so shadows have a soft penumbra instead of a
 hard edge. This is the reference site's "ray traced shadows" technique, from
 Codex [Device] AST. The soft-shadow sampler and the per-sample occlusion test
 are tail-recursive folds the plug lowers to nested WGSL loops. Real math from
 Gpu chapter DeviceMath.

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  sd-width : Integer = 1024
  sd-half-w : Integer = 512
  sd-half-h : Integer = 384
  sd-nobj : Integer = 4
  sd-samples : Integer = 9

Section: Scene Table

  sd-cx : Integer -> Real
  sd-cx (i) = if i == 0 then 0.0 else if i == 1 then 0.0 - 1.7 else 1.6

  sd-cy : Integer -> Real
  sd-cy (i) = if i == 0 then 0.0 else if i == 1 then 0.0 - 0.35 else 0.0 - 0.45

  sd-cz : Integer -> Real
  sd-cz (i) = if i == 0 then 0.0 else if i == 1 then 0.5 else 0.0 - 0.4

  sd-rad : Integer -> Real
  sd-rad (i) = if i == 0 then 1.0 else if i == 1 then 0.65 else 0.55

  sd-col-r : Integer -> Real
  sd-col-r (i) = if i == 0 then 0.90 else if i == 1 then 0.35 else 0.80

  sd-col-g : Integer -> Real
  sd-col-g (i) = if i == 0 then 0.55 else if i == 1 then 0.75 else 0.45

  sd-col-b : Integer -> Real
  sd-col-b (i) = if i == 0 then 0.35 else if i == 1 then 0.55 else 0.95

Section: Intersection

  sd-sphere-hit : Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> Real
  sd-sphere-hit (ox) (oy) (oz) (dx) (dy) (dz) (i) =
    let lx = ox - sd-cx i
    in let ly = oy - sd-cy i
    in let lz = oz - sd-cz i
    in let b = dx * lx + dy * ly + dz * lz
    in let r = sd-rad i
    in let c = lx * lx + ly * ly + lz * lz - r * r
    in let disc = b * b - c
    in if disc < 0.0 then 0.0 - 1.0
    else let t = 0.0 - b - real-sqrt disc
    in if t > 0.001 then t else 0.0 - 1.0

  sd-plane-hit : Real, Real -> Real
  sd-plane-hit (oy) (dy) =
    if dy > 0.0 - 0.0001 then 0.0 - 1.0
    else let t = (0.0 - 1.0 - oy) / dy
    in if t > 0.001 then t else 0.0 - 1.0

  sd-hit : Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> Real
  sd-hit (ox) (oy) (oz) (dx) (dy) (dz) (id) =
    if id == 3 then sd-plane-hit oy dy
    else sd-sphere-hit ox oy oz dx dy dz id

  sd-nearest : Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Integer, Integer, Real -> Integer
  sd-nearest (ox) (oy) (oz) (dx) (dy) (dz) (i) (best-id) (best-t) =
    if i >= sd-nobj then best-id
    else let t = sd-hit ox oy oz dx dy dz i
    in let take = if t > 0.001 then (if best-t < 0.0 then 1 else if t < best-t then 1 else 0) else 0
    in if take == 1 then sd-nearest ox oy oz dx dy dz (i + 1) i t
    else sd-nearest ox oy oz dx dy dz (i + 1) best-id best-t

Section: Soft Shadow

 The occlusion test: any sphere hit along the shadow ray blocks the sample.

  sd-occluded : Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Integer -> Integer
  sd-occluded (ox) (oy) (oz) (dx) (dy) (dz) (i) =
    if i >= 3 then 0
    else let t = sd-sphere-hit ox oy oz dx dy dz i
    in if t > 0.001 then 1
    else sd-occluded ox oy oz dx dy dz (i + 1)

 Light samples: a 3x3 grid across a disk at height 6, radius ~1.1.

  sd-off-x : Integer -> Real
  sd-off-x (i) = real-from-int (i - (i / 3) * 3 - 1) * 1.1

  sd-off-z : Integer -> Real
  sd-off-z (i) = real-from-int (i / 3 - 1) * 1.1

 Fold over the 9 light samples, counting how many are visible from the hit
 point (each is a normalized shadow ray toward that light-disk point). The disk
 is centred at (lx, 6, lz), which orbits with the frame so the shadows sweep.

  sd-soft : Real, Real, Real, Real, Real, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sd-soft (hx) (hy) (hz) (lx) (lz) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= sd-samples then acc
    else let ddx = lx + sd-off-x i - hx
    in let ddy = 6.0 - hy
    in let ddz = lz + sd-off-z i - hz
    in let dl = real-sqrt (ddx * ddx + ddy * ddy + ddz * ddz)
    in let ux = ddx / dl
    in let uy = ddy / dl
    in let uz = ddz / dl
    in let occ = sd-occluded (hx + ux * 0.003) (hy + uy * 0.003) (hz + uz * 0.003) ux uy uz 0
    in let vis = if occ == 1 then 0 else 1
    in sd-soft hx hy hz lx lz (i + 1) (acc + vis)

Section: Shading

  sd-clamp01 : Real -> Real
  sd-clamp01 (x) = real-max 0.0 (real-min 1.0 x)

  sd-pack : Real, Real, Real -> Integer
  sd-pack (r) (g) (b) =
    let ri = real-to-int (sd-clamp01 r * 255.0)
    in let gi = real-to-int (sd-clamp01 g * 255.0)
    in let bi = real-to-int (sd-clamp01 b * 255.0)
    in ri * 65536 + gi * 256 + bi

  sd-sky : Real -> Integer
  sd-sky (dy) =
    let h = sd-clamp01 (dy * 0.5 + 0.5)
    in sd-pack (0.06 + h * 0.07) (0.10 + h * 0.15) (0.24 + h * 0.40)

  sd-checker : Real, Real -> Real
  sd-checker (hx) (hz) =
    let ix = real-to-int (hx + 64.0)
    in let iz = real-to-int (hz + 64.0)
    in let s = ix + iz
    in if s - (s / 2) * 2 == 0 then 0.38 else 0.66

Section: Render

 Per pixel: primary ray, nearest hit, Lambert toward the light centre scaled by
 the fraction of the light disk that is visible (the soft shadow term).

  sd-render : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sd-render (gid) (frame) =
    let px = gid - (gid / sd-width) * sd-width
    in let py = gid / sd-width
    in let fx = real-from-int (px - sd-half-w) / 384.0
    in let fy = real-from-int (sd-half-h - py) / 384.0
    in let rl = real-sqrt (fx * fx + fy * fy + 2.89)
    in let dx = fx / rl
    in let dy = fy / rl
    in let dz = 1.7 / rl
    in let ox = 0.0
    in let oy = 0.7
    in let oz = 0.0 - 4.0
    in let id = sd-nearest ox oy oz dx dy dz 0 (0 - 1) (0.0 - 1.0)
    in if id < 0 then sd-sky dy
    else let t = sd-hit ox oy oz dx dy dz id
    in let hx = ox + dx * t
    in let hy = oy + dy * t
    in let hz = oz + dz * t
    in let nx = if id == 3 then 0.0 else (hx - sd-cx id) / sd-rad id
    in let ny = if id == 3 then 1.0 else (hy - sd-cy id) / sd-rad id
    in let nz = if id == 3 then 0.0 else (hz - sd-cz id) / sd-rad id
    in let br = if id == 3 then sd-checker hx hz else sd-col-r id
    in let bg = if id == 3 then sd-checker hx hz else sd-col-g id
    in let bb = if id == 3 then sd-checker hx hz else sd-col-b id
    in let ang = real-from-int frame / 30.0
    in let lx = real-cos ang * 3.0
    in let lz = real-sin ang * 3.0
    in let lcx = lx - hx
    in let lcy = 6.0 - hy
    in let lcz = lz - hz
    in let lcl = real-sqrt (lcx * lcx + lcy * lcy + lcz * lcz)
    in let ndl = real-max 0.0 (nx * lcx / lcl + ny * lcy / lcl + nz * lcz / lcl)
    in let vis = real-from-int (sd-soft hx hy hz lx lz 0 0) / 9.0
    in let lit = 0.18 + ndl * 0.92 * vis
    in sd-pack (br * lit) (bg * lit) (bb * lit)

Section: Shadow Kernel

  shadow-step : Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device] Integer
  shadow-step (outb) (frame) (gid) = act
    device-store outb gid (sd-render gid frame)
  end
